---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Viva Talent | Carlos Menco Guardo" mainClass="main-content main-content--project-detail" activePage="vivatalent" pageScripts={["/js/project-scroll-gradient.js"]}>
  <div class="content--sidebar">
    <div class="project-header">
      <div class="project-img-wrapper">
        <img src="/imgs/vivatalent-preview.png" alt="Viva Talent redesign proposal preview" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="s1">
      <span class="project-detail-year">2026</span>
      <h5 class="project-detail-title">Viva Talent Redesign Proposal</h5>
      <p class="project-detail-description">A website redesign proposal for a talent and executive assistant brand, built with WordPress, ACF, GSAP, and Lottie to create a more polished, flexible, and story-driven experience.</p>
      <a href="https://vivatalent.carlosmenco.site/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="external-link">View proposal <span class="external-link-icon"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M4.22876 4.22924V5.5586L9.49435 5.56332L3.75736 11.3003L4.70017 12.2431L10.4372 6.50613L10.4324 11.7717H11.7712V4.22924H4.22876Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></span></a>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Overview</h6>
      <p>Viva Talent is a redesign proposal focused on improving how a service-based talent brand communicates trust, process, and value. The project follows a similar direction to the ABA Centers proposal: cleaner content structure, stronger presentation, and a more maintainable WordPress foundation.</p>
      <p>The site was planned around flexible content sections that can support marketing pages, service explanations, case studies, and conversion-focused landing pages without requiring a full rebuild every time the message changes.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Role</h6>
      <p>Website redesign, WordPress architecture, ACF content modeling, frontend implementation, GSAP interaction planning, Lottie integration, responsive refinement, and Codex-assisted development.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Challenge</h6>
      <p>The proposal needed to make a professional services offer feel clear, premium, and easy to understand. It also needed to give the client a practical editing workflow so the site could keep evolving after launch.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Solution</h6>
      <ul>
        <li>Structured the site around service clarity, brand trust, and conversion paths.</li>
        <li>Used WordPress with ACF to keep content modular and editor-friendly.</li>
        <li>Planned GSAP and Lottie motion for key moments without making the experience feel heavy.</li>
        <li>Kept the frontend flexible enough for future landing pages, campaign pages, and content updates.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Outcome</h6>
      <p>The result is a more modern redesign direction that gives the brand room to communicate expertise, guide prospects through the offer, and manage future content with less friction.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
